---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SectionHeading from '../../../components/ui/SectionHeading.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../../../components/navigation/Breadcrumb.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../../../config/site';

const locale = 'en' as const;
---

<BaseLayout
  locale={locale}
  path="/en/privacy/"
  otherLocalePath="/zh-tw/privacy/"
  title="Privacy Policy (Portfolio Demo) | FORGEON AUTOMATION"
  description="How the FORGEON AUTOMATION portfolio demo site's RFQ form actually handles your data: this is a concept demonstration site, and form data is never sent, transmitted, or stored on any server."
>
  <div class="container section--tight">
    <Breadcrumb locale={locale} items={[{ label: 'Privacy Policy', path: '/en/privacy/' }]} />
  </div>

  <section class="section section--tight">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <SectionHeading
        level="h1"
        eyebrow="Privacy Policy"
        title="What Actually Happens to Data You Type Into This Form"
        description="This document describes the actual behavior of this portfolio concept site, not a translated template of a generic corporate privacy policy."
      />

      <div class="privacy-notice">
        <p><strong>Concept case disclosure:</strong> "FORGEON AUTOMATION" is a fictional portfolio concept case built by Yegou Studio (頁構所) for market validation, not a real operating company. This page exists to demonstrate the complete information architecture a real B2B site needs, including a consent checkbox that links to an actual, real page, rather than to serve as a legally reviewed compliance document.</p>
      </div>

      <h2>What actually happens to Demo Mode form submissions</h2>
      <p class="measure">
        The <a href="/en/contact/">Contact &amp; RFQ form</a> on this site currently runs in Demo Mode: it performs full client-side validation in your browser (required fields, email format, minimum requirement-description length, and so on), but once validation passes, <strong>no field data is transmitted to any server</strong> and no network request of any kind is made. Everything you type exists only in your current browser tab's memory; refreshing the page discards it. No database, spreadsheet, or CRM ever receives it.
      </p>
      <p class="measure">
        If the <code>PUBLIC_RFQ_ENDPOINT</code> environment variable is later set to a real API endpoint (switching the site to Live Mode), the form will <code>fetch()</code> your field data as JSON to that endpoint. Before any real production launch, the site operator is responsible for replacing this page with a legally reviewed privacy policy that discloses actual data retention periods, any third-party processors, and how users can exercise access, correction, and deletion rights.
      </p>

      <h2>What kind of information the form asks for</h2>
      <p class="measure">
        Company name, contact name, job title, email, phone, country/region, industry, project type, requirement description, target timeline, budget range, and checkbox fields for whether you already have technical specifications or require an NDA. These fields are designed so a sales or engineering team could do a first-pass qualification before ever making contact (see <a href="/en/about/">About</a>). In Demo Mode, as described above, none of it leaves your browser.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies and tracking</h2>
      <p class="measure">
        No real GTM tracking ID is wired into this codebase (<code>PUBLIC_GTM_ID</code> is blank in the example environment file; it is also the only analytics script path this codebase actually loads). The site has an account-agnostic event layer (<code>window.dataLayer</code>) that only loads any tracking script once a site operator sets a real GTM container ID; during this portfolio demonstration phase, no third-party tracking service is loaded and no cookies are set.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p class="measure">
        Questions about how this demo site handles privacy, or interested in the real privacy policy template Yegou Studio provides for actual client engagements, can be sent to <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.contact.emailEn}`}>{siteConfig.contact.emailEn}</a> (demo address).
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .container--narrow {
    max-width: 720px;
  }
  .privacy-notice {
    background: var(--color-surface-alt);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-strong);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: var(--space-md);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
  }
  .privacy-notice p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: var(--fs-lg);
    margin: var(--space-xl) 0 var(--space-sm);
  }
  p.measure {
    color: var(--color-muted);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-md);
  }
  code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.9em;
    background: var(--color-surface-alt);
    padding: 0.1em 0.35em;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  }
</style>
